WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.025
To close: decisions, vendor
asks, and next steps.

2
00:00:04.025 --> 00:00:05.500
The decisions to take.

3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.312
Which servers run in FIPS mode, and
which separate servers run ACME.

4
00:00:10.312 --> 00:00:14.886
Whether database secrets are protected
by an HSM or by the software key,

5
00:00:14.886 --> 00:00:17.599
and whether SQL is Enterprise or Standard.

6
00:00:17.599 --> 00:00:22.412
Console sign-in through Entra single sign-on
with certificate-based authentication.

7
00:00:22.412 --> 00:00:26.163
The public CA path, if the
agency uses Entrust today.

8
00:00:26.163 --> 00:00:29.318
Whether to build the Cloud
PKI feed on a beta API,

9
00:00:29.318 --> 00:00:31.988
and whether to adopt the ServiceNow app.

10
00:00:31.988 --> 00:00:36.376
Ask CyberArk, in writing: which
statement governs ACME and FIPS;

11
00:00:36.376 --> 00:00:41.354
whether AD CS on Windows Server 2025
is supported, given the stale table;

12
00:00:41.354 --> 00:00:44.560
which cryptographic
module the product uses,

13
00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:50.044
and whether any CMVP certificate covers
it; whether the Key Vault driver works

14
00:00:50.044 --> 00:00:55.613
with Azure Government; and whether PIV or
CAC console login is supported as such.

15
00:00:55.613 --> 00:01:00.466
Next steps: stand up the Wave 1
test cluster, create the CA account

16
00:01:00.466 --> 00:01:05.412
under the ESC7 controls, and lab-test
allowed and denied requests.

17
00:01:05.412 --> 00:01:12.669
The Federal Modernization Workbook's Book
07 has been updated in Chapters 03 and 05

18
00:01:12.669 --> 00:01:17.402
for the ESC7 caveat, Chapter
04 for Cloud PKI reporting,

19
00:01:17.402 --> 00:01:20.137
and Chapter 08 for ACME and FIPS.

20
00:01:20.137 --> 00:01:24.937
The program's recommendation is
plain: CyberArk Certificate Manager,

21
00:01:24.937 --> 00:01:28.826
Self-Hosted, is the right
platform for Book 07's lifecycle.

22
00:01:28.826 --> 00:01:33.072
It's the agency's existing
machine-identity vendor, it covers every

23
00:01:33.072 --> 00:01:37.550
issuer the design assigns to it, and
its risks are known and manageable.

24
00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:39.614
The backup slides list the risks,

25
00:01:39.614 --> 00:01:42.900
the assessor evidence and
what couldn't be verified.

26
00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:45.940
This is the program's
research, under review,

27
00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:48.812
not an endorsement by any federal agency.

28
00:01:48.812 --> 00:01:49.574
Thank you.

29
00:01:49.574 --> 00:01:57.842
Sources: Research brief sections 0,
12 and 13; Book 07, Chapters 03,

30
00:01:57.842 --> 00:02:06.000
04, 05, 07 and 08; CyberArk 26.1
documentation cited in Parts 1 to 3.
